.TH TTMP "1" "2026-10-08" "ttmp 0.3.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ttmp \- minimal TUI music player that organizes songs using tags.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ttmp
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR | \fI\,FILE\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
All arguments that do not start with a '-' will be interpreted as file paths.
If you specify at least 1 file, you will (unless specified otherwise) start in 'temp' mode
with all of those songs in the current playlist.
Otherwise, you will start in 'main' mode, restoring your previous main mode playlist.
.PP
If the first file argument is an absolute path, IPC will be enabled,
which will send any songs to an already open ttmp process (if one exists).
.PP
To get started with ttmp, run \fBttmp\fR and then press '?' or ':help first<Enter>'
to get an introduction on how to use ttmp.
.PP
You can set the path to your music folder in \fI\,files.ron\/\fR in the data directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-help, \-h\fP
Print help and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version, \-v\fP
Print version info and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\-ipc\fP
Force interprocess communication to be enabled.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-ipc\fP
Disable all interprocess communication.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-media\fP
Disable media controls and metadata.
.TP
\fB\-\-mode, \-m\fP \fI\,MODE\/\fR
Specify what program mode to start in.
\fI\,MODE\/\fR must be either 'main' or 'temp'.

Main mode is the typical mode in which you can listen to the
songs in your music folder and your last session is restored.

In temp mode, pressing 'r' will only fill the playlist with the songs given in the
command line arguments and no operation will save anything to the config or data paths.
Do note that default config and data are still created if they don't already exist.
.TP
\fB\-\-data, \-d\fP \fI\,PATH\/\fR
Specify the data path.
\fI\,PATH\/\fR should be a directory.

The default data path is \fI\,$XDG_DATA_HOME/ttmp\/\fR or \fI\,~/.local/share/ttmp\/\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-config, \-c\fP \fI\,PATH\/\fR
Specify the config path.
\fI\,PATH\/\fR should be a directory.

The default config path is \fI\,$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ttmp\/\fR or \fI\,~/.config/ttmp\/\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-\fP
Force all arguments after this one to be interpreted as file paths.
.SH BUGS
.PP
The text "audio stream error: Buffer underrun/overrun occurred." will sometimes be displayed.
This is a bug in one of ttmp's dependencies.
If you resize the terminal window, everything will be redrawn, which will clear this text.
.PP
You can report bugs at: \fI\,https://github.com/BlueSheep3/ttmp/issues\/\fR
